<h1>Donna Miller</h1>
<p>US House, 2nd District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic.</p>
<p><a href="https://donnaforcongress.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (donnaforcongress.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Her campaign&#39;s priorities page lists healthcare under a Medicare for All framework, lowering prescription drug costs and capping insulin prices, maternal health and reproductive rights, jobs and lower costs, climate, a path to citizenship with due process protections, gun laws and violence prevention, voting rights, veterans, and protecting Social Security. In her Chicago Sun-Times questionnaire she says health care is the major thread running through her district&#39;s issues and that she would work to restore Affordable Care Act tax credits.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Cook County Commissioner for the 6th district since 2018, previously a healthcare and pharmaceutical industry consultant and account specialist and board chair of Planned Parenthood Illinois.</p>
